    "type": "question",
    "label": "81",
    "prompt": "Given a set $X$, its $\\mathit{power\\ set}$, $\\mathcal P(X)$, is the set containing all subsets of $X$. Write down $\\mathcal P(X)$ for\n$$X=\\{x,y,z\\}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\mathcal P(X)=\\{\\varnothing,\\{x\\},\\{y\\},\\{z\\},\\{x,y\\},\\{x,z\\},\\{y,z\\},\\{x,y,z\\}\\}$.\n\nList subsets by size: $1+3+3+1=8$ subsets.",
      "worked": "List subsets with zero, one, two and three elements. Order within a subset does not matter.\n$$\\mathcal P(X)=\\bigl\\{\\varnothing,\\{x\\},\\{y\\},\\{z\\},\\{x,y\\},\\{x,z\\},\\{y,z\\},\\{x,y,z\\}\\bigr\\}.$$\nThere are $1+3+3+1=8$ subsets.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
